    {
      "slug": "boyaryna-morozova-painting",
      "title": "Boyaryna Morozova (painting)",
      "year": 1887,
      "imageUrl": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/Vasily_Surikov_-_%D0%91%D0%BE%D1%8F%D1%80%D1%8B%D0%BD%D1%8F_%D0%9C%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BE%D0%B7%D0%BE%D0%B2%D0%B0_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg",
      "imageWidth": 4000,
      "imageHeight": 2059,
      "story": "Boyaryna Morozova is a painting by V. I. Surikov, measuring 304 by 587.5 cm, depicts a scene from the history of the church schism in the 17th century. After its debut at the 15th Travelling Exhibition in 1887, it was purchased for 25 thousand rubles for the Tretyakov Gallery, where it remains one of the main exhibits.",
      "facts": [
        "Surikov recalled that the key to the image of the protagonist was inspired by a crow with a black wing, which was once seen beating against the snow.",
        "The artist attached the sketches to the painting with buttons, which left holes that were discovered during restoration.",
        "In the color of the Russian winter, the artist's eye first discovered an inexhaustible richness."
      ],
      "wikipediaUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boyaryna_Morozova_(painting)",
